h notebook and workbench images to rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal | Implementation | Notebooks | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8001-E007 | Switch serving and training runtime images to rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal | Implementation | Model Serving | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8001-E008 | Switch python-variant-based images to PQC python base variants | Implementation | Model Serving | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8001-E009 | Dashboard nodejs-22 image PQC remediation | Implementation | Dashboard | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8001-E010 | fms-guardrails-orchestrator ML-KEM TLS stack migration | Implementation | AI Guardrails | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8001-E011 | Trainer data cache PQC remediation | Implementation | Model Training | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8001-E012 | PQC compliance verification CI scan for the RHOAI 3.6 payload | Implementation | DevOps Build | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8001-E013 | TLS handshake performance regression validation | Implementation | PerfScale | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8001-E014 | PQC compliance coordination and tracking | Implementation | DevOps Build / PM | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8001-E015 | PQC Readiness Matrix and base image switch documentation | Implementation (docs-authoring) | Documentation | P2 |\n\n## Dependency DAG\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\nE001[RHAISTRAT-8001-E001] --> E008\nE001 --> E009\nE002[RHAISTRAT-8001-E002] --> E011\nE003[RHAISTRAT-8001-E003] --> E006\nE003 --> E007\nE004[RHAISTRAT-8001-E004] --> E015\nE005[RHAISTRAT-8001-E005] --> E015\nE006 --> E015\nE007 --> E015\nE008 --> E015\nE009 --> E015\nE010[RHAISTRAT-8001-E010] --> E015\nE011 --> E015\nE012[RHAISTRAT-8001-E012] --> E015\nE013[RHAISTRAT-8001-E013] --> E015\nE014[RHAISTRAT-8001-E014] --> E015\n```\n\nArrows point from dependency to dependent (`E003 --> E006` means E003 must complete before E006 starts).\n\n## DAG Justification\n\n| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n|------|------|-----------|\n| E001 → E008 | Rule 3 (Investigation gates) | Whether PQC python base variants exist (and by when) determines whether the python-variant-based images can switch or must go the OCP-exception path. True gate: `remove` if variants are not available in time. |\n| E001 → E009 | Rule 3 (Investigation gates) | The dashboard nodejs-22 base is \"PQC variant or exception\"; the variant-availability outcome selects switch vs exception. True gate: `remove` (exception fallback). |\n| E002 → E011 | Rule 3 (Investigation gates) | The TLS-stack audit determines whether the trainer data cache inherits PQC from the base image (no remediation) or needs TLS-stack remediation / an OCP exception. True gate: `add_remediation`. |\n| E003 → E006 | Rules 3, 16, 18 | The AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase (AIPCC-7258) is an external dependency with uncertain timing that gates rhel9-8-els adoption; the go/no-go decision determines whether the notebook/workbench images switch or file exceptions. Tier 2 work. |\n| E003 → E007 | Rules 3, 16, 18 | Same rebase gate for the serving/training runtime images currently on rhel9-6-els. |\n| all Implementation epics (E004–E014) → E015 | Rule 11 (docs last) | The PQC Readiness Matrix and documentation describe what was built; docs-authoring is blocked by every Implementation epic. |\n| E004 ∥ E005 (no edge) | Rules 13, 14 | Base image availability is already confirmed (registry images exist); build-pipeline consumability is a configuration reference — an AC gate on the switch epics, not a DAG dependency. |\n| E005 ∥ E012 (no edge) | Rule 15 | The verification scan tooling is built in parallel with the switches; first meaningful execution is gated by the scan's own AC (switched images present in the payload). |\n| E005 ∥ E006/E007/E008/E009 (no edge) | Rules 14, 15 | Different image groups/repos; PQC base availability is a confirmed configuration input, not a build-against artifact. |\n| E010, E013, E014 roots (no edges) | Rules 14, 17 | The fms-guardrails TLS migration, performance validation, and compliance coordination deliver independent value and are not gated by any in-strategy epic (RHOAIENG-7452 spike and RHAISTRAT-7816 are external). |\n\n## HLR Traceability Matrix\n\n| HLR | Priority | Epics |\n|-----|----------|-------|\n| All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image (ubi9-minimal-pqc, rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal, or equivalent) for RHOAI 3.6 / OCP 5.0 | P0 | E004 (enables), E005 (ubi9-minimal wave, ~68 images), E006 (notebooks/workbenches), E007 (runtimes/mlserver), E008 (python-based images), E009 (dashboard), E010 (fms-guardrails remediation), E011 (trainer data cache remediation); verified by E012 |\n| Teams unable to comply by September 15 must file an OCP exception with a remediation plan | P0 | E014 (aggregated tracking, zero unaccounted images) + exception-fallback acceptance criteria on E006, E008, E009, E010, E011. Individual exception filings are owned by each team and are explicitly out of strategy scope. |\n| PQC enablement is runtime only — only the final stage of the Dockerfile/Containerfile changes; no builder image change | P0 | E005 (primary: runtime-stage-only scope constraint); the same constraint is carried in the scope of E006–E009 |\n| PQC-signed X.509 certificates (ML-DSA) | Deferred | Out of scope — no epic (follow-on phase per strategy) |\n\nFull coverage: no orphaned HLRs. HLR-4 is explicitly deferred by the strategy.\n\n## Tiered Delivery\n\nExternal dependencies with uncertain timing (AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase, python/nodejs PQC variants) allow partial value without them:\n\n- **Tier 1 (independent, start immediately)**: E001, E002, E003 (investigations), E004 (pipeline/build config), E005 (~68 ubi9-minimal-based images on the confirmed `ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc`), E010, E011 (remediations), E012 (verification scan), E013 (performance validation), E014 (coordination).\n- **Tier 2 (dependency-gated)**: E006, E007 (gated by the RHEL 9.8 rebase go/no-go), E008, E009 (gated by PQC variant availability). If a gate resolves negatively, the affected images fall back to the OCP-exception path (HLR-2) tracked by E014 — no unaccounted images.\n\n## Component Mapping Notes\n\nCanonical component names taken verbatim from `.context/rhai-components.txt`:\n\n- **E005** spans many strategy components (Go operators and platform components, ~68 images). Assigned the single most-relevant canonical name `OpenShift AI Productization`; per-team execution is delegated via tracking tickets linked to the parent strategy per the strategy's own coordination model.\n- **E007/E008** span serving and training runtime images (mlserver, training runtimes, training variants, lmes-job, feature-server). Assigned `Model Runtimes`; the feature-server image is Feature Store territory and lmes-job is AI Evaluations territory, but a single image each does not warrant separate epics.\n- **E002/E011** (trainer / trainer-operator / trainer data cache): the canonical list has no \"Trainer\" component; mapped to `Model Customization` as the closest canonical name covering model training work.\n- **E014** (coordination) mapped to `AI Platform DevOps`.\n\n## Health Warnings\n\n- **Performance NFR lacks a numeric threshold** — the strategy flags \"NEEDS DOMAIN INPUT\" (owner: PM + Performance team lead, due before Sprint 2 ends). Captured as an acceptance criterion on E013 (threshold agreed and documented before measurement); flagged for human verification.\n- **TrustyAI explainability has no remediation epic** — Java/NSS TLS stack, remediation tied to the JDK 29 LTS timeline (September 2027). Per the strategy an OCP exception is expected; the filing is team-owned and out of scope. Compliance for this image is covered only via E014 tracking — a multi-release compliance gap worth leadership visibility.\n- **Priority judgment call (possible inversion)**: E010 (fms-guardrails) and E011 (trainer data cache) remediations are P1 although HLR-1 is P0. Rationale: the September 15 deadline for these components is met via the HLR-2 exception path; the migrations are the remediation those exceptions commit to. If product decides the migrations must land in 3.6, raise both to P0.\n- **FIPS + PQC incompatibility**: on FIPS-mode clusters, FIPS policy deactivates PQC for this release — expected behavior, documented as a note in E012's acceptance criteria, not a compliance failure.\n- **E005 spans multiple teams**: the strategy delegates per-image switches to component teams via linked tracking tickets; the epic is the coordination wave, and its completion is measured through those tickets plus the payload scan.\n- **Pending process gates**: Architecture Review, ODH/RHOAI Build Onboarding, Licence Validation, and Documentation Support are all \"Pending human review\" in the strategy — flagged for human follow-up; no onboarding chain epics were generated because all affected components already have architecture context (in platform).\n- **Out-of-scope boundary honored**: individual-team OCP exception filings, Go ML-KEM / TLSAdherence / TLS-scanner CI (RHAISTRAT-7816), and post-OCP-5.0 base image evolution are excluded from this decomposition.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":52805,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b82c88193c77520","agent_id":"ae447954eeaf34fb2","session_id":"f2d69f1c-9b04-453b-94d6-4bb7c2d36986","uuid":"9e19da21-4eeb-46ec-87e8-b951ac8117fe","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:23:26.611Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8001"}
