{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-b2f95953-72c4-4ea5-a505-22409359eb85","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b75ebfa8a4c9f41","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8001-sg79b66w/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8001-E001.md","content":"# Confirm PQC base image variants for python-311/312, python-312-minimal, and nodejs-22\n\n## Description\n\nResolve whether PQC-enabled variants of the `ubi9/python-311`, `ubi9/python-312`, `ubi9/python-312-minimal`, and `ubi9/nodejs-22` base images exist or will be delivered in time for the September 15, 2026 RHOAI 3.6 deadline. This investigation tracks and consolidates the outcome of the AIPCC spike RHOAIENG-7195 and produces a per-variant verdict (available with registry coordinates, committed delivery date, or not planned) that determines whether the roughly ten images built on those bases switch to a PQC variant or fall back to the OCP-exception path.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Confirm current registry availability of PQC variants for `ubi9/python-311`, `ubi9/python-312`, `ubi9/python-312-minimal`, and `ubi9/nodejs-22` (pull candidates and verify `update-crypto-policies --show` reports `DEFAULT:PQ` where present).\n- Obtain from the AIPCC team a committed delivery date for each variant that is not yet published, escalating if no committed date exists by early September (per the strategy's risk mitigation).\n- Produce a per-variant decision record: switch (variant and coordinates) or exception (affected images and owning teams).\n- Identify the affected images per variant from the RHOAI 3.5 image inventory: training variants and lmes-job on python-311 (5 images), training variants on python-312 (4 images), feature-server on python-312-minimal (1 image), and the dashboard on nodejs-22 (1 image).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A decision record exists listing each of the four base variants with one of: available now (with registry coordinates and verified `DEFAULT:PQ` policy), committed delivery date on or before September 15, 2026, or not available (exception path).\n- Each affected image is mapped to exactly one variant verdict and an owning team.\n- The verdict is communicated to the affected teams and to the compliance coordination effort in time to act before the deadline.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 [P0]: All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image — this investigation resolves the availability unknown for the python/nodejs-based images.\n- HLR-2 [P0]: Teams unable to comply by September 15 must file an OCP exception — the verdict identifies which teams must file.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":57232,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b82c88193c77520","agent_id":"ae447954eeaf34fb2","session_id":"f2d69f1c-9b04-453b-94d6-4bb7c2d36986","uuid":"6b3fd353-36b6-4607-b1f7-3e6da534b723","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:23:42.685Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8001"}
