{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-b2f95953-72c4-4ea5-a505-22409359eb85","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-acf50cfa327c40ef","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8001-sg79b66w/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8001-E002.md","content":"# Audit trainer data cache Rust TLS stack posture\n\n## Description\n\nDetermine the TLS stack posture of the trainer data cache component: whether it uses system OpenSSL via a native-tls stack (and therefore inherits PQC from a PQC-enabled base image) or a pure-Rust TLS stack such as rustls with the ring provider (which cannot inherit PQC from a base image swap and would need remediation or an OCP exception). This resolves the unknown tracked by audit spike RHOAIENG-7196.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Audit the trainer data cache source and dependency tree (Cargo dependency graph, TLS client/server construction sites) to identify the concrete TLS stack in use.\n- Classify the outcome: OpenSSL/native-tls backed (base image switch is sufficient) versus pure-Rust TLS stack (remediation or exception required).\n- If a pure-Rust TLS stack is found, characterize the migration surface (which crates and call sites) so the remediation can be scoped.\n- Document the finding and the resulting compliance path for the component.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A written audit record identifies the TLS stack of the trainer data cache with concrete evidence (dependency and source references).\n- The record states one of: PQC inherited from the PQC base image (no remediation needed), or remediation required (with the affected crates/call sites enumerated).\n- The finding is handed to the component team and the compliance coordination effort.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 [P0]: All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image — this audit determines whether the base image switch actually delivers ML-KEM capability for this component.\n- HLR-2 [P0]: Teams unable to comply by September 15 must file an OCP exception — the audit outcome decides whether this component is on the switch path or the exception path.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":57232,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b82c88193c77520","agent_id":"ae447954eeaf34fb2","session_id":"f2d69f1c-9b04-453b-94d6-4bb7c2d36986","uuid":"d0c1366b-d654-4ee6-8c21-bcfb54b862a8","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:23:50.209Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8001"}
