characteristics change.\n- Until remediated (if required), the team's OCP exception documents the TLS stack and this remediation plan.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 [P0]: All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image — delivers or verifies ML-KEM capability for this component per the audit outcome.\n- HLR-2 [P0]: Teams unable to comply by September 15 must file an OCP exception — the exception path applies if remediation is needed but not complete.\n- NFR (Security — PQC algorithm compliance, non-Go components): any Rust component using a pure-Rust TLS stack must support ML-KEM hybrid key exchange after migration.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":63143,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b82c88193c77520","agent_id":"ae447954eeaf34fb2","session_id":"f2d69f1c-9b04-453b-94d6-4bb7c2d36986","uuid":"35f0d1fb-fdbf-40bb-9051-38d67374a2b9","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:25:12.513Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8001"}
