{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-0a360dd7-b468-4bdc-9de7-2384fb4bf64f","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-af8d801e1fe49c12","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8001-sg79b66w/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8001-E012.md","content":"# PQC compliance verification CI scan for the RHOAI 3.6 payload\n\n## Description\n\nBuild and run the automated CI scan that measures PQC base image compliance across the RHOAI 3.6 payload, implementing the strategy's acceptance criterion: for every OpenSSL-backed runtime image, `update-crypto-policies --show` reports `DEFAULT:PQ` and `openssl list -kem-algorithms` lists ML-KEM-512, ML-KEM-768, and ML-KEM-1024. The scan produces the per-image compliance record that feeds the aggregated tracking view and identifies any unaccounted-for images.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Implement a payload scan (CI job) that, for each image in the RHOAI 3.6 payload: runs `update-crypto-policies --show` and `openssl list -kem-algorithms` inside the container and records the result.\n- Classify each image: PQC-compliant (OpenSSL-backed, DEFAULT:PQ), exception-covered (non-OpenSSL TLS stack with a filed OCP exception), or unaccounted.\n- Exclude non-OpenSSL TLS stack components (rustls+ring, Java/NSS) from the algorithm check — those are covered by exception filings, not the scan.\n- Record the known FIPS-mode caveat: on FIPS-mode clusters, FIPS policy deactivates PQC in this release; DEFAULT:PQ being non-functional on FIPS clusters is expected and is not a compliance failure for RHOAI 3.6.\n- Run the scan across the full payload and publish the per-image results.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The scan executes in CI against the RHOAI 3.6 payload and produces a per-image report of crypto policy and ML-KEM algorithm availability.\n- Every image in the payload is classified as compliant, exception-covered, or unaccounted — the report enumerates zero unaccounted images when the deadline is met, or names them otherwise.\n- Non-OpenSSL components are handled per the exclusion rule rather than failing the scan.\n- The FIPS-cluster caveat is recorded in the scan output so FIPS-mode results are not misread as failures.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 [P0]: All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image — this scan is the automated measurement of that requirement across the payload.\n- HLR-2 [P0]: Teams unable to comply by September 15 must file an OCP exception — the scan's exception-covered/unaccounted classification feeds the zero-unaccounted-images check.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":63143,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b82c88193c77520","agent_id":"ae447954eeaf34fb2","session_id":"f2d69f1c-9b04-453b-94d6-4bb7c2d36986","uuid":"aab38251-0b0e-41a8-b369-9ac7e0895661","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:25:21.109Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8001"}
