{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-0a360dd7-b468-4bdc-9de7-2384fb4bf64f","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bc062b460f65de61","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8001-sg79b66w/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8001-E013.md","content":"# TLS handshake performance regression validation\n\n## Description\n\nMeasure the TLS handshake latency impact of the PQC base image switch and the ML-KEM hybrid key exchange across representative RHOAI component images, against an agreed numeric regression threshold, fulfilling the strategy's Performance NFR (flagged \"NEEDS DOMAIN INPUT\" — the threshold must be set by the PM and performance team lead before measurement) and the Performance Team Support prerequisite.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Agree and document the numeric TLS handshake latency regression threshold with the PM and performance team lead (the strategy's open domain input; reference points: Chrome ~10% maximum TLS handshake time regression, PSASTRAT-7170 Red Hat PQC benchmarking outcome).\n- Benchmark TLS handshake latency before and after the PQC switch for representative switched components (a Go operator/platform component, a Python component, and a native-tls Rust component).\n- Measure both PQC-negotiating (hybrid X25519MLKEM768) and classic ECDHE handshakes, since non-PQC clients continue to be supported.\n- Report the measured regression against the threshold and flag any component exceeding it.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A documented, agreed numeric regression threshold exists (signed off by PM and performance team lead) before measurements are taken.\n- Before/after handshake latency measurements exist for the representative component set, covering both hybrid and classic key exchange.\n- The measured regression is reported against the threshold, with any exceeding component flagged for remediation.\n- No HA characteristics change as a result of the switch (no additional replicas required) — confirmed in the report.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- NFR (Performance): TLS handshake regression must be measured before ship — this epic is that measurement.\n- HLR-1 [P0]: supports the payload-wide base image switch by validating its performance acceptability.\n\n## Risks\n\n- The threshold decision requires PM and performance team lead input (human gate); the strategy requires it before Sprint 2 ends.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":63143,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b82c88193c77520","agent_id":"ae447954eeaf34fb2","session_id":"f2d69f1c-9b04-453b-94d6-4bb7c2d36986","uuid":"aa89a9a6-318f-4199-9830-34c81c1a016b","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:25:28.221Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8001"}
