{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad2a453915c7c777","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8001-E003\n3\ttitle: RHEL 9.8 ELS rebase timing and rhel9-8-els adoption go/no-go\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8001\n5\tcomponent: AIPCC Productization\n6\tteam: AIPCC\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 0\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: 0\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# RHEL 9.8 ELS rebase timing and rhel9-8-els adoption go/no-go\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolve whether the AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase (AIPCC-7258) — which gates adoption of the `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal` base image — will land in time for RHOAI 3.6, and produce a go/no-go decision for switching the roughly 34 images currently built on `rhel9-6-els` bases (notebooks, workbenches, training runtimes, mlserver) to `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal`. A no-go routes those images to the OCP-exception path for this release.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Track the AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase (AIPCC-7258) committed dates and slip risk against the September 15, 2026 deadline.\n34\t- Verify the `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal` image remains available and reports `DEFAULT:PQ` (confirmed available per OCPSTRAT-7413 correspondence, August 2026).\n35\t- Produce a go/no-go decision for rhel9-8-els adoption in RHOAI 3.6, with the affected image list and owning teams for each outcome.\n36\t- Define the decision date after which a no-go defaults affected teams to the OCP-exception path.\n37\t\n38\t## Acceptance Criteria\n39\t\n40\t- A decision record exists stating go or no-go for rhel9-8-els adoption in RHOAI 3.6, with the evidence (rebase dates, image availability verification) attached.\n41\t- The roughly 34 affected images on rhel9-6-els bases are enumerated with owning teams.\n42\t- The decision is communicated to affected teams and the compliance coordination effort before the deadline, leaving enough time to file exceptions on a no-go.\n43\t\n44\t## HLR Traceability\n45\t\n46\t- HLR-1 [P0]: All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image — this decision gates the switch path for all rhel9-6-els-based images.\n47\t- HLR-2 [P0]: Teams unable to comply by September 15 must file an OCP exception — a no-go outcome identifies the teams that must file.\n48\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bfbd7b3ae971b896","agent_id":"a3c5157a286246483","session_id":"f2d69f1c-9b04-453b-94d6-4bb7c2d36986","uuid":"28c6f03c-3e81-4c9d-82fb-0b66aeb2e084","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:29:38.892Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad2a453915c7c777","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8001 decomposition"}
