{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bec8bc8533321749","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8001-E005\n3\ttitle: Switch ubi9-minimal-based platform images to ubi9-minimal-pqc\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8001\n5\tcomponent: OpenShift AI Productization\n6\tteam: DevOps Build\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: -1\n18\t  repo_access: 0\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 4\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Switch ubi9-minimal-based platform images to ubi9-minimal-pqc\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tComplete the switch wave for the roughly 68 RHOAI component images currently built on `ubi9/ubi-minimal:latest` bases — Go operators and most platform components — to the confirmed PQC base image `registry.redhat.io/ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc`. Only the final runtime stage of each Dockerfile/Containerfile changes; no builder image change is needed. Per the strategy's coordination model, per-image execution is owned by the component teams through their tracking tickets linked to the parent strategy; this epic drives, aggregates, and completes the wave.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Enumerate the ubi9-minimal-based images from the RHOAI 3.5 CSV relatedImages list and the organized image inventory.\n38\t- Coordinate with each owning team (or execute directly for shared/midstream build configurations) to switch the final runtime stage of each image to `ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc`.\n39\t- Track per-image completion status through team tracking tickets linked to the parent strategy for OCP 5.0 aggregated visibility.\n40\t- Images that a team cannot switch by September 15, 2026 are routed to the OCP-exception path with a documented remediation plan (filing owned by the team, tracked by the compliance coordination effort).\n41\t- Go components gain ML-KEM via native Go crypto regardless; the base switch is done for platform consistency per the strategy's confirmed assumption.\n42\t\n43\t## Acceptance Criteria\n44\t\n45\t- Every ubi9-minimal-based image in the RHOAI 3.6 payload either builds on `ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc` or has a team-filed OCP exception with a remediation plan.\n46\t- For each switched image, `update-crypto-policies --show` inside the running container reports `DEFAULT:PQ`, and `openssl list -kem-algorithms` lists ML-KEM-512, ML-KEM-768, and ML-KEM-1024.\n47\t- No Dockerfile/Containerfile builder stage was modified as part of the switch (runtime stage only).\n48\t- Rollback path: each switched image's previous base reference is recoverable (base references are pinned and reversible, no feature flag required for a base image revert).\n49\t\n50\t## HLR Traceability\n51\t\n52\t- HLR-1 [P0]: All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image — covers the ~68 ubi9-minimal-based images.\n53\t- HLR-2 [P0]: Teams unable to comply by September 15 must file an OCP exception — non-switchable images are routed to the exception path.\n54\t- HLR-3 [P0]: PQC enablement is runtime only — the scope explicitly limits changes to the final runtime stage.\n55\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bfbd7b3ae971b896","agent_id":"a3c5157a286246483","session_id":"f2d69f1c-9b04-453b-94d6-4bb7c2d36986","uuid":"0ed37586-df15-4fc1-a7ca-32d3f61e2e5c","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:29:40.266Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bec8bc8533321749","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8001 decomposition"}
