{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8981dd07ede6d8d8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8001-E006\n3\ttitle: Switch notebook and workbench images to rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8001\n5\tcomponent: Notebooks Images\n6\tteam: Notebooks\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8001-E003\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8001-E003\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: remove\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the RHEL 9.8 rebase does not land in time (no-go), the notebook\n15\t    and workbench images stay on rhel9-6-els for RHOAI 3.6 and the owning teams file\n16\t    OCP exceptions with documented remediation plans per HLR-2.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 1\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: 0\n23\t  external_dependency: -1\n24\t  human_process_gates: 0\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: High\n30\tai_implementability_score: 4\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Switch notebook and workbench images to rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tSwitch the notebook and code-server workbench images currently built on `rhel9-6-els` bases to `registry.redhat.io/rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal`, changing only the final runtime stage of each image. This work is gated on the go/no-go decision for rhel9-8-els adoption, which depends on the AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase (AIPCC-7258).\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Switch the final runtime stage of all notebook and workbench image variants (JupyterLab and code-server families, CPU and accelerator variants) from `rhel9-6-els` bases to `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal`.\n43\t- Re-verify the image test suite (container tests, culling API behavior) against the new base, since the RHEL 9.8 ELS base carries a newer runtime than 9.6.\n44\t- Keep hermetic RPM and Python dependency management unchanged; only the base image reference in the runtime stage changes.\n45\t- If the adoption go/no-go decision is no-go, or the switch cannot complete by September 15, 2026, support the owning teams' OCP-exception filings with the TLS stack documentation and remediation plan (deadline compliance via exception for this release).\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- Every notebook and workbench image in the RHOAI 3.6 payload builds on `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal` (runtime stage only), or has a filed OCP exception with a remediation plan.\n50\t- `update-crypto-policies --show` reports `DEFAULT:PQ` inside each switched image; the Python `cryptography` library continues to work against the system OpenSSL on the new base.\n51\t- The existing container test suite passes on the new base.\n52\t- The PQC base image is consumable through the RHOAI build pipeline (build pipeline gate).\n53\t- Rollback path: the previous rhel9-6-els base reference remains restorable.\n54\t\n55\t## HLR Traceability\n56\t\n57\t- HLR-1 [P0]: All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image — covers the notebook/workbench images on rhel9-6-els bases.\n58\t- HLR-2 [P0]: Teams unable to comply by September 15 must file an OCP exception — no-go/late outcomes route to the exception path.\n59\t- HLR-3 [P0]: PQC enablement is runtime only — final runtime stage only, no builder image change.\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bfbd7b3ae971b896","agent_id":"a3c5157a286246483","session_id":"f2d69f1c-9b04-453b-94d6-4bb7c2d36986","uuid":"5d117ec9-fca5-4a39-b74e-7c87af2e78dc","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:29:43.640Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8981dd07ede6d8d8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8001 decomposition"}
