{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-95a3145212491c11","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8001-E013\n3\ttitle: TLS handshake performance regression validation\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8001\n5\tcomponent: PerfScale\n6\tteam: PerfScale\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: -1\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: -1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: Medium\n23\tai_implementability_score: 2\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# TLS handshake performance regression validation\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tMeasure the TLS handshake latency impact of the PQC base image switch and the ML-KEM hybrid key exchange across representative RHOAI component images, against an agreed numeric regression threshold, fulfilling the strategy's Performance NFR (flagged \"NEEDS DOMAIN INPUT\" — the threshold must be set by the PM and performance team lead before measurement) and the Performance Team Support prerequisite.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Agree and document the numeric TLS handshake latency regression threshold with the PM and performance team lead (the strategy's open domain input; reference points: Chrome ~10% maximum TLS handshake time regression, PSASTRAT-7170 Red Hat PQC benchmarking outcome).\n38\t- Benchmark TLS handshake latency before and after the PQC switch for representative switched components (a Go operator/platform component, a Python component, and a native-tls Rust component).\n39\t- Measure both PQC-negotiating (hybrid X25519MLKEM768) and classic ECDHE handshakes, since non-PQC clients continue to be supported.\n40\t- Report the measured regression against the threshold and flag any component exceeding it.\n41\t\n42\t## Acceptance Criteria\n43\t\n44\t- A documented, agreed numeric regression threshold exists (signed off by PM and performance team lead) before measurements are taken.\n45\t- Before/after handshake latency measurements exist for the representative component set, covering both hybrid and classic key exchange.\n46\t- The measured regression is reported against the threshold, with any exceeding component flagged for remediation.\n47\t- No HA characteristics change as a result of the switch (no additional replicas required) — confirmed in the report.\n48\t\n49\t## HLR Traceability\n50\t\n51\t- NFR (Performance): TLS handshake regression must be measured before ship — this epic is that measurement.\n52\t- HLR-1 [P0]: supports the payload-wide base image switch by validating its performance acceptability.\n53\t\n54\t## Risks\n55\t\n56\t- The threshold decision requires PM and performance team lead input (human gate); the strategy requires it before Sprint 2 ends.\n57\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bfbd7b3ae971b896","agent_id":"a3c5157a286246483","session_id":"f2d69f1c-9b04-453b-94d6-4bb7c2d36986","uuid":"0ae1cd33-5ee6-4de4-8d6b-55d4a47caa0b","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:29:51.687Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-95a3145212491c11","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8001 decomposition"}
