ation outcome.\n41\t- Verify at the deadline that zero unaccounted images remain.\n42\t\n43\t## Acceptance Criteria\n44\t\n45\t- Every image in the RHOAI 3.6 payload is represented by a team tracking ticket linked to the parent strategy (aggregated compliance view exists for OCP 5.0).\n46\t- By September 15, 2026: every image is classified as rebuilt on a PQC-enabled base or covered by a filed-and-acknowledged OCP exception with a remediation plan that names the component's TLS stack — zero unaccounted images.\n47\t- Reminder cadence and escalation actions are logged (weekly reminders; leadership escalation for at-risk teams).\n48\t\n49\t## HLR Traceability\n50\t\n51\t- HLR-2 [P0]: Teams unable to comply by September 15 must file an OCP exception with a remediation plan — this epic drives and verifies that guarantee.\n52\t- HLR-1 [P0]: All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image — the aggregated view tracks per-image completion of the switch wave.\n53\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bfbd7b3ae971b896","agent_id":"a3c5157a286246483","session_id":"f2d69f1c-9b04-453b-94d6-4bb7c2d36986","uuid":"a79a6a30-787a-40ea-929b-82e98178f438","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:29:52.378Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bdb9788b8c683608","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8001 decomposition"}
