e dashboard's TLS stack (Node.js TLS, traffic largely fronted by the Go proxy) and remediation plan to support the team's OCP-exception filing.\n44\t- Confirm the dashboard's end-to-end TLS posture (browser to Go proxy to dashboard) is documented for the compliance record either way.\n45\t\n46\t## Acceptance Criteria\n47\t\n48\t- The dashboard image in the RHOAI 3.6 payload either builds on a PQC nodejs variant (runtime stage only) or has a filed OCP exception documenting the TLS stack and remediation plan.\n49\t- If switched: `update-crypto-policies --show` reports `DEFAULT:PQ` inside the image and existing dashboard validation passes on the new base.\n50\t- The documented TLS posture covers the Go-proxy-fronted path, so the compliance record shows which hop is PQC-capable.\n51\t\n52\t## HLR Traceability\n53\t\n54\t- HLR-1 [P0]: All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image — covers the dashboard image.\n55\t- HLR-2 [P0]: Teams unable to comply by September 15 must file an OCP exception — the no-variant outcome routes this image to the exception path.\n56\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b1e60a45d5b7e82d","agent_id":"a9d1a007d1727a349","session_id":"f2d69f1c-9b04-453b-94d6-4bb7c2d36986","uuid":"7e7b07e1-ba63-4ad2-8800-34ed61b2d3e8","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:36:05.514Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-81cb2fe2bed96929","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8001 decomposition"}
