{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-acdbc95600373ce1","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8001-E014\n3\ttitle: PQC compliance coordination and tracking\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8001\n5\tcomponent: AI Platform DevOps\n6\tteam: DevOps Build\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 0\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: -1\n18\t  repo_access: 0\n19\t  architecture_claims: 0\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: Medium\n23\tai_implementability_score: 1\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# PQC compliance coordination and tracking\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tRun the compliance coordination this strategy exists to provide: aggregate every component team's PQC base image switch or OCP exception status through tracking tickets linked to the parent strategy, drive teams toward the September 15, 2026 deadline with weekly reminders and escalation, and maintain the zero-unaccounted-images guarantee for OCP 5.0 visibility.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Ensure every RHOAI component team has a tracking ticket linked to the parent strategy, covering each image in the RHOAI 3.5 CSV relatedImages inventory (153 images).\n38\t- Maintain the aggregated compliance view: per image, switched / in-progress / exception-filed / unaccounted.\n39\t- Send weekly reminders to teams without a resolution path; escalate to leadership per the sync decision for teams at risk of missing the deadline without an exception.\n40\t- Track exception status for the known non-OpenSSL components (fms-guardrails-orchestrator, TrustyAI explainability) and for any team routed to the exception path by a negative investigation outcome.\n41\t- Verify at the deadline that zero unaccounted images remain.\n42\t\n43\t## Acceptance Criteria\n44\t\n45\t- Every image in the RHOAI 3.6 payload is represented by a team tracking ticket linked to the parent strategy (aggregated compliance view exists for OCP 5.0).\n46\t- By September 15, 2026: every image is classified as rebuilt on a PQC-enabled base or covered by a filed-and-acknowledged OCP exception with a remediation plan that names the component's TLS stack — zero unaccounted images.\n47\t- Reminder cadence and escalation actions are logged (weekly reminders; leadership escalation for at-risk teams).\n48\t\n49\t## HLR Traceability\n50\t\n51\t- HLR-2 [P0]: Teams unable to comply by September 15 must file an OCP exception with a remediation plan — this epic drives and verifies that guarantee.\n52\t- HLR-1 [P0]: All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image — the aggregated view tracks per-image completion of the switch wave.\n53\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b1e60a45d5b7e82d","agent_id":"a9d1a007d1727a349","session_id":"f2d69f1c-9b04-453b-94d6-4bb7c2d36986","uuid":"dc6dc304-ad45-4dd3-9fc4-463108fa18c9","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:36:12.077Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-acdbc95600373ce1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8001 decomposition"}
