{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9140fe2c920aae82","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8001-E001\n3\ttitle: Confirm PQC base image variants for python-311/312, python-312-minimal, and\n4\t  nodejs-22\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8001\n6\tcomponent: AIPCC Ecosystems\n7\tteam: AIPCC Base Images\n8\ttype: Investigation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies: []\n11\tinvestigation_signals:\n12\t  question_specificity: 1\n13\t  source_accessibility: 1\n14\t  local_runnability: 1\n15\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n16\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n17\timplementation_type: null\n18\tai_signals: null\n19\tai_implementability: Medium\n20\tai_implementability_score: 2\n21\tjira_key: null\n22\tbranch: null\n23\tgated_by: null\n24\tgate_failure_impact: null\n25\t---\n26\t# Confirm PQC base image variants for python-311/312, python-312-minimal, and nodejs-22\n27\t\n28\t## Description\n29\t\n30\tResolve whether PQC-enabled variants of the `ubi9/python-311`, `ubi9/python-312`, `ubi9/python-312-minimal`, and `ubi9/nodejs-22` base images exist or will be delivered in time for the September 15, 2026 RHOAI 3.6 deadline. This investigation tracks and consolidates the outcome of the AIPCC spike RHOAIENG-7195 and produces a per-variant verdict (available with registry coordinates, committed delivery date, or not planned) that determines whether the roughly ten images built on those bases switch to a PQC variant or fall back to the OCP-exception path.\n31\t\n32\t## Scope\n33\t\n34\t- Confirm current registry availability of PQC variants for `ubi9/python-311`, `ubi9/python-312`, `ubi9/python-312-minimal`, and `ubi9/nodejs-22` (pull candidates and verify `update-crypto-policies --show` reports `DEFAULT:PQ` where present).\n35\t- Obtain from the AIPCC team a committed delivery date for each variant that is not yet published, escalating if no committed date exists by early September (per the strategy's risk mitigation).\n36\t- Produce a per-variant decision record: switch (variant and coordinates) or exception (affected images and owning teams).\n37\t- Identify the affected images per variant from the RHOAI 3.5 image inventory: training variants and lmes-job on python-311 (5 images), training variants on python-312 (4 images), feature-server on python-312-minimal (1 image), and the dashboard on nodejs-22 (1 image).\n38\t\n39\t## Acceptance Criteria\n40\t\n41\t- A decision record exists listing each of the four base variants with one of: available now (with registry coordinates and verified `DEFAULT:PQ` policy), committed delivery date on or before September 15, 2026, or not available (exception path).\n42\t- Each affected image is mapped to exactly one variant verdict and an owning team.\n43\t- The verdict is communicated to the affected teams and to the compliance coordination effort in time to act before the deadline.\n44\t\n45\t## HLR Traceability\n46\t\n47\t- HLR-1 [P0]: All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image — this investigation resolves the availability unknown for the python/nodejs-based images.\n48\t- HLR-2 [P0]: Teams unable to comply by September 15 must file an OCP exception — the verdict identifies which teams must file.\n49\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b1e60a45d5b7e82d","agent_id":"a9d1a007d1727a349","session_id":"f2d69f1c-9b04-453b-94d6-4bb7c2d36986","uuid":"7f301dc3-64cc-4d59-bd67-a90598686487","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:36:12.688Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9140fe2c920aae82","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8001 decomposition"}
