{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b48dcffa299b1054","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8001-E004\n3\ttitle: PQC base image pipeline and build configuration updates\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8001\n5\tcomponent: Build and Release\n6\tteam: DevOps Build\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# PQC base image pipeline and build configuration updates\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tMake the PQC-enabled base images consumable by the RHOAI build infrastructure: update shared build configurations, base image reference templates, and pipeline inputs so component teams can build their images against `ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc` and `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal`. This is the DevOps/Build team's coordinated pipeline update named in the strategy's impacted teams.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Update RHOAI build configuration repositories and shared base image reference variables to include the PQC base images (`ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc`, `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal`).\n38\t- Verify the PQC base images are pullable through the build pipeline (registry access, digests, multi-arch availability for amd64/ppc64le/s390x where components ship multi-arch).\n39\t- Provide the standard final-runtime-stage switch pattern (runtime stage only, no builder image change) for component teams to apply.\n40\t- Consume the RHEL 9.8 ELS rebase go/no-go outcome (produced by the dedicated rebase-timing investigation) to decide when the `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal` reference is enabled in shared build configuration; this epic does not re-track the rebase itself.\n41\t\n42\t## Acceptance Criteria\n43\t\n44\t- A test build using each PQC base image succeeds through the standard RHOAI build pipeline, on every architecture the payload ships.\n45\t- Component teams can select the PQC base images via the shared build configuration mechanism without pipeline changes of their own.\n46\t- The runtime-stage-only switch pattern is documented and published to component teams.\n47\t- Rollback path: the previous non-PQC base image references remain restorable in the build configuration (no destructive replacement).\n48\t\n49\t## HLR Traceability\n50\t\n51\t- HLR-1 [P0]: All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image — this epic makes the PQC bases consumable for every component switch.\n52\t- HLR-3 [P0]: PQC enablement is runtime only — the published switch pattern covers only the final runtime stage.\n53\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f9b93b48fa20659","agent_id":"ab172bc4e60960384","session_id":"f2d69f1c-9b04-453b-94d6-4bb7c2d36986","uuid":"d1e86e9a-815c-44ff-9917-ff8e558097aa","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:38:18.685Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b48dcffa299b1054","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8001 decomposition"}
