{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a5dcea5b167bb06b","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8001-E005\n3\ttitle: Switch ubi9-minimal-based platform images to ubi9-minimal-pqc\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8001\n5\tcomponent: OpenShift AI Productization\n6\tteam: DevOps Build\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: -1\n18\t  repo_access: 0\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 4\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Switch ubi9-minimal-based platform images to ubi9-minimal-pqc\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tComplete the switch wave for the roughly 68 RHOAI component images currently built on `ubi9/ubi-minimal:latest` bases — Go operators and most platform components — to the confirmed PQC base image `registry.redhat.io/ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc`. Only the final runtime stage of each Dockerfile/Containerfile changes; no builder image change is needed. Per the strategy's coordination model, per-image execution is owned by the component teams through their tracking tickets linked to the parent strategy; this epic drives, aggregates, and completes the wave.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Enumerate the ubi9-minimal-based images from the RHOAI 3.5 CSV relatedImages list and the organized image inventory.\n38\t- Coordinate with each owning team (or execute directly for shared/midstream build configurations) to switch the final runtime stage of each image to `ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc`.\n39\t- Surface per-image completion status through the single aggregated compliance view maintained by the PQC compliance coordination effort (one view over the team tracking tickets linked to the parent strategy, for OCP 5.0 visibility); this epic does not maintain a separate wave-status tracker.\n40\t- Images that a team cannot switch by September 15, 2026 are routed to the OCP-exception path with a documented remediation plan (filing owned by the team, tracked by the compliance coordination effort).\n41\t- Go components gain ML-KEM via native Go crypto regardless; the base switch is done for platform consistency per the strategy's confirmed assumption.\n42\t\n43\t## Acceptance Criteria\n44\t\n45\t- Every ubi9-minimal-based image in the RHOAI 3.6 payload either builds on `ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc` or has a team-filed OCP exception with a remediation plan.\n46\t- Execution is explicitly subordinated to team tickets: each image's switch is executed and closed through the owning component team's tracking ticket linked to the parent strategy (DevOps Build executes directly only shared/midstream build configurations); this epic completes when every ticket in the wave is resolved as switched or exception-filed.\n47\t- For each switched image, `update-crypto-policies --show` inside the running container reports `DEFAULT:PQ`, and `openssl list -kem-algorithms` lists ML-KEM-512, ML-KEM-768, and ML-KEM-1024.\n48\t- No Dockerfile/Containerfile builder stage was modified as part of the switch (runtime stage only).\n49\t- Rollback path: each switched image's previous base reference is recoverable (base references are pinned and reversible, no feature flag required for a base image revert).\n50\t\n51\t## HLR Traceability\n52\t\n53\t- HLR-1 [P0]: All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image — covers the ~68 ubi9-minimal-based images.\n54\t- HLR-2 [P0]: Teams unable to comply by September 15 must file an OCP exception — non-switchable images are routed to the exception path.\n55\t- HLR-3 [P0]: PQC enablement is runtime only — the scope explicitly limits changes to the final runtime stage.\n56\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f9b93b48fa20659","agent_id":"ab172bc4e60960384","session_id":"f2d69f1c-9b04-453b-94d6-4bb7c2d36986","uuid":"3d8e713b-0569-44b8-aea2-76fa8a9eda46","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:38:19.482Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a5dcea5b167bb06b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8001 decomposition"}
