{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b1aec7fd44fa57c","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8001-E012\n3\ttitle: PQC compliance verification CI scan for the RHOAI 3.6 payload\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8001\n5\tcomponent: Build and Release\n6\tteam: DevOps Build\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 7\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# PQC compliance verification CI scan for the RHOAI 3.6 payload\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tBuild and run the automated CI scan that measures PQC base image compliance across the RHOAI 3.6 payload, implementing the strategy's acceptance criterion: for every OpenSSL-backed runtime image, `update-crypto-policies --show` reports `DEFAULT:PQ` and `openssl list -kem-algorithms` lists ML-KEM-512, ML-KEM-768, and ML-KEM-1024. The scan produces the per-image compliance record that feeds the aggregated tracking view and identifies any unaccounted-for images.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Implement a payload scan (CI job) that, for each image in the RHOAI 3.6 payload: runs `update-crypto-policies --show` and `openssl list -kem-algorithms` inside the container and records the result.\n38\t- Classify each image: PQC-compliant (OpenSSL-backed, DEFAULT:PQ), exception-covered (non-OpenSSL TLS stack with a filed OCP exception), or unaccounted.\n39\t- Exclude non-OpenSSL TLS stack components (rustls+ring, Java/NSS) from the algorithm check — those are covered by exception filings, not the scan.\n40\t- Record the known FIPS-mode caveat: on FIPS-mode clusters, FIPS policy deactivates PQC in this release; DEFAULT:PQ being non-functional on FIPS clusters is expected and is not a compliance failure for RHOAI 3.6.\n41\t- Run the scan across the full payload and publish the per-image results.\n42\t\n43\t## Acceptance Criteria\n44\t\n45\t- The scan executes in CI against the RHOAI 3.6 payload and produces a per-image report of crypto policy and ML-KEM algorithm availability.\n46\t- Every image in the payload is classified as compliant, exception-covered, or unaccounted — the report enumerates zero unaccounted images when the deadline is met, or names them otherwise.\n47\t- Non-OpenSSL components are handled per the exclusion rule rather than failing the scan.\n48\t- The FIPS-cluster caveat is recorded in the scan output so FIPS-mode results are not misread as failures.\n49\t\n50\t## HLR Traceability\n51\t\n52\t- HLR-1 [P0]: All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image — this scan is the automated measurement of that requirement across the payload.\n53\t- HLR-2 [P0]: Teams unable to comply by September 15 must file an OCP exception — the scan's exception-covered/unaccounted classification feeds the zero-unaccounted-images check.\n54\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f9b93b48fa20659","agent_id":"ab172bc4e60960384","session_id":"f2d69f1c-9b04-453b-94d6-4bb7c2d36986","uuid":"f88e724f-5819-4081-b262-4b321b701ef3","timestamp":"2026-10-22T07:38:32.843Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b1aec7fd44fa57c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8001 decomposition"}
